(in-ns 'go.arbace.hs) ^{:go/comments [[15 1 "// Frame is a frame of a thread's stack (HES8 (a))."] [19 15 "// a case's slots; an apply frame's arguments"] [22 11 "// the thread's arena's top when the frame was pushed (arena.go)"] [30 8 "// restores the masking state n on return"] [35 8 "// keepAlive#'s value kept reachable while its action runs"] [38 1 "// Thread is a Haskell thread: its stack, its resumption, its masking state (0 unmasked, 1 masked"] [39 1 "// uninterruptibly, 2 masked interruptibly: getMaskingState#'s numbers)."] [50 23 "// what it waits on: *MVar, *Thunk, *sleep, stmWait, nil when runnable"] [51 23 "// the throwTo#s waiting for it to accept them (rts.go)"] [52 23 "// the TVars its transaction read (a retry's wake-up, the collector's reachability)"] [59 2 "// an interruptible block (MVar, delay, STM retry): an asynchronous exception may be delivered"] [63 1 "// Machine is hsi's machine: the loader, the address space, the threads."] [78 2 "// the weak pointers not yet dead, and the collector's memos of what code keeps alive (rts.go)"] [97 49 "// a pure primop's arguments"] [98 49 "// a thread's frames at most (SetStackLimit): StackOverflow past it"] [99 49 "// a tail call's arguments"] [112 1 "// hsFatal is an error of hsi itself (a class at the check: unimplemented, an impossible state)."] [115 1 "// exitNow ends the program (shutdownHaskellAndExit, an uncaught exception in the main thread)."] [122 1 "// NewMachine is a machine over the STG of the units in libs and the program in prog."] [161 1 "// blockedE is returned by a node whose thread blocked: its resumption is set already."] [164 1 "// enterValue evaluates a value: a thunk entered, anything else returned."] [173 1 "// enter evaluates a thunk: its value, or its code under an update frame, the thunk blackholed."] [191 3 "// another thread evaluates it: wait for its update; a transaction aborts first and reruns from its start"] [192 3 "// after the wake-up (review 189, F2, the user's decision: the other threads never see its writes)"] [210 4 "// two update frames in a row (the lower thunk's evaluation is entering this one): squeezed as GHC's"] [211 4 "// stack squeezing does, the lower thunk an indirection to this one, one frame for both (cgrun060 at"] [212 4 "// +RTS -K64k)"] [213 4 "// (the lower thunks kept blackholed in the frame's env, updated, raised or reverted with it)"] [221 4 "// evaluated in place (newThunkN)"] [230 1 "// update overwrites a thunk with its value."] [234 30 "// the fields and the frame may live in the thunk's own allocation"] [245 1 "// apply calls f with args (eval/apply: exact, partial, over-saturated)."] [285 1 "// ApplyV applies a value to values (a thread's start, a primop's callback)."] [295 1 "// ret handles the top frame on a return."] [313 4 "// a queued throwTo# delivered at the unmasking, its value lost as GHC's"] [326 1 "// raiseLam is the code of a thunk whose evaluation raised: entered, it raises again."] [329 1 "// RaiseFree raises its frame's first slot."] [336 1 "// raise raises a synchronous exception (raise#, raiseIO#): the stack unwound to the nearest catch"] [337 1 "// frame, the thunks under evaluation on the way updated to raise it again."] [342 1 "// raiseAsync raises an asynchronous exception in the current thread: the thunks under evaluation on"] [343 1 "// the way reverted to unevaluated (GHC freezes them; the same results)."] [370 5 "// an asynchronous exception is not catchSTM#'s: its nested writes undone, on (review 189, F9)"] [385 1 "// uncaught ends a thread whose exception reached the bottom of its stack (forkIO's and runMainIO's own"] [386 1 "// handlers catch everything, so only a thread started without them gets here: one killed before it ran,"] [387 1 "// which ends silently, as GHC's)."] [395 2 "// a thread killed before it started (forkIO's handler not yet on its stack) ends silently, as GHC's"] [398 1 "// ---- threads ----"] [408 1 "// wake makes a blocked thread runnable."] [418 1 "// block stops the current thread until it is woken; on waking it returns from the blocked call"] [419 1 "// (with the return registers its waker sets) or runs e."] [426 3 "// a queued throwTo# delivered as the thread blocks interruptibly (threadPaused's"] [427 3 "// maybePerformBlockedException; review 189, F5)"] [435 1 "// unblock takes a blocked thread out of what it waits on."] [468 3 "// its throwTo# revoked"] [473 2 "// an interrupted MVar operation leaves no state (review 189, F4)"] [479 1 "// Run runs the program's :Main.main and returns its exit status."] [517 1 "// where describes the current thread's stack for an error message."] [544 1 "// schedule runs threads until until is done (or every thread is)."] [595 1 "// deadlock is GHC's scheduleDetectDeadlock when no thread can run and none waits for time: a collection (rts.go's"] [596 1 "// gc) resurrects the blocked threads no root reaches; when it resurrects none, the main thread, blocked, gets"] [597 1 "// NonTermination (the non-threaded RTS's last resort). False: nothing to do (hsi stops)."] [609 1 "// runSlice runs t for a time slice, or until it blocks or ends."] [622 5 "// GHC's threadStackOverflow: StackOverflow raised in the thread, asynchronously"] [626 39 "// a transaction is not preempted (HES9 (a))"] [646 1 "// shutdown flushes the standard handles (hs_exit's flushStdHandles) and is the exit status."] [658 1 "// Exit is the program's end requested by shutdownHaskellAndExit: the handles flushed first."] [672 1 "// CFunctions are the C functions hsi's table has."] [681 1 "// PrimopNames are the primops hsi implements."] [690 1 "// Loaded is the number of modules loaded, LoadedBytes their forms' size, Steps the nodes run (by slices)."] [695 1 "// defaultStackFrames is a thread's frames at most without -K: 2 GiB of frames (GHC's default is 80 % of the host's"] [696 1 "// memory, which hsi's frames, larger than GHC's words, would reach later than GHC; a bound keeps an endless recursion"] [697 1 "// from taking the host: the review of HE4d's runs). Loop's 3,000,000-deep chain needs about 10 million."] [700 1 "// frameBytes is a frame's size, the unit -K's bytes are counted in (GHC counts its stack's words; a frame of hsi's"] [701 1 "// holds what a few of GHC's words do, so a -K limit is reached at a comparable depth, not the same one)."] [704 1 "// SetStackLimit sets a thread's stack limit to bytes (+RTS -K)."] [713 1 "// unwindThunk is a thunk under evaluation an exception unwinds: reverted to unevaluated (asynchronous), or made to raise"] [714 1 "// again (synchronous); its waiters woken."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[166 24] [178 27] [209 18] [237 23] [314 36] [374 37] [428 35] [486 20] [526 27] [526 44] [602 17] [724 24]]} (go/file "machine.go" :imports [


